{
    "background_story": "Kobe was a gentle dormouse who lived in a cozy nest at the heart of a lush forest. As a member of the gliridae family, he was well adapted to his nocturnal lifestyle, spending most of his days snuggled up in his nest, sleeping. But when night fell, Kobe transformed into a nimble and curious explorer, venturing out to discover the forest's secrets. With his large, round eyes and agile limbs, he navigated the trees with ease, feasting on juicy fruits and nuts. Kobe's love for gliding through the forest canopy earned him the nickname 'Moon Whisperer' among his fellow dormice. Despite his love for solitude, Kobe had a soft spot for his neighbor, a wise old owl named Hootie, with whom he shared tales of his nocturnal adventures.",
